{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 7.169,
   "text": "When I was nine, my dad had one rule for our house."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 7.769,
   "end": 11.289,
   "text": "The hallway light stays on all night. Always."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 11.889,
   "end": 17.756,
   "text": "And if you ever wake up and it's off... don't get out of bed. Don't call for us. Just wait for morning."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 18.356,
   "end": 20.959,
   "text": "I thought he was scared of burglars."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 21.959,
   "end": 27.036,
   "text": "Then, one night in December, I woke up... and the crack under my door was black."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 28.636,
   "end": 35.569,
   "text": "Somewhere out in the dark hall, I heard my mom's voice. Honey? The power's out. Come here, I've got a flashlight."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 36.169,
   "end": 40.735,
   "text": "But there was no flashlight beam. Not under the door. Not anywhere."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 41.735,
   "end": 45.831,
   "text": "So I pulled the blanket over my head... and I didn't answer."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 47.231,
   "end": 52.863,
   "text": "The voice came closer. Right outside my door. It's okay, sweetheart. It's just me."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.063,
   "end": 58.265,
   "text": "It kept saying that... over and over... until the sun came up."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 60.665,
   "end": 64.591,
   "text": "At breakfast, Mom swore she'd slept straight through the night."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 65.391,
   "end": 72.473,
   "text": "Dad didn't say a word. He just got the stepladder from the garage, climbed all the way up, and screwed the bulb back in."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 73.673,
   "end": 78.964,
   "text": "Our ceilings are ten feet high. Whatever loosened that bulb... didn't need a ladder."
  }
 ],
